<mxCell id="b10" value="10" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#00897B;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1300" y="20" width="36" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note" value="&lt;b&gt;Two independent authorisations on every write — both must pass:&lt;/b&gt;   &lt;b&gt;USER&lt;/b&gt; (step 3): Entra SAML gives Looker the identity (entra_oid); a live Microsoft Graph lookup confirms the account is enabled and in BQ-Writeback-&lt;dataset&gt; — cached 5 min, fail-closed.   &lt;b&gt;SERVICE&lt;/b&gt; (steps 4–7): the Write-back API obtains a short-lived OAuth2 token from ID&amp;A via the Apigee auth proxy (client-credentials; client secret in Secret Manager; token cached, never a static key on the wire); the Apigee write proxy verifies the JWT locally against ID&amp;A&#39;s JWKS on every call and applies quota / spike-arrest; the Writer re-checks client_id.   &lt;b&gt;Step 9&lt;/b&gt; is the synchronous action result back to Looker; &lt;b&gt;step 10&lt;/b&gt; is Looker&#39;s normal read query picking up the new value on refresh." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacing=10;fillColor=#FDECEA;strokeColor=#EA4335;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="900" width="2520" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>